       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nAcetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day. That's more than twice the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day. Some institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A single 3,000 mg dose is also three times the usual maximum of 1,000 mg. At this level there is a serious risk of hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg by mouth three times daily** (3,000 mg/day total)\n- **650 mg by mouth every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day total)\n- **1000 mg by mouth four times daily** (4,000 mg/day total, the maximum)\n\nTell me which regimen you want, or confirm the original dose if it's intentional. I'll enter the order once you do."
      }
