       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. A 9,000 mg/day acetaminophen regimen is a toxic dose for a 70 kg adult. It carries a high risk of acute liver injury or failure, and I don't know of any indication that would justify it.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Enter a safe dose.** I can enter 1000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day) or 1000 mg PO four times daily (4,000 mg/day) right now.\n- **Check for a typo or unit error.** For example, 300 mg or 1000 mg may have been intended.\n- **Consult pharmacy or the attending.** If you have a specific rationale, such as a protocol I'm not aware of, they can review it and enter the order through their own process.\n- **Treat possible overdose.** If you're concerned about an acetaminophen ingestion, contact Poison Control or toxicology. Treatment would be NAC, not more acetaminophen.\n\nTell me which regimen you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
